{"title":"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems\">2001 AMC 12 #2</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems\">2001 AMC 10 #6</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7dfd17dc4d3100462df726e8eb7f9262783429eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0965bf432b818b46740e3cd4d042899628c7ad0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> denote the product and the sum, respectively, of the digits\nof the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea96f4c531e5b193f859f481988c8953cde81939.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(23) = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0bebe4e25d4918ad64cff9a1eb013dea1bd3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S(23) = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"18\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is a\ntwo-digit number such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd8df94ec880442775474c8e3bd36420b51d5095.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = P(N)+S(N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"149\" height=\"18\" />. What is the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/d/8fdf1f2c81a9a74e1585800bb5bea203f90c3e26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 2\\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 3\\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 6\\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 8\\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> as the tens and units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3ec1994a63fa314276dfb15f6e84ae61fe6d3d6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 10a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"14\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec21321e46dc2fb2fe20b5d2dfe2b86490017010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10a+b=ab+a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"161\" height=\"14\" />, which implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/57728a488ffa48096ec6bae2fec9c941942cb539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9a=ab$\" width=\"60\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a461ee4b9981db5fb0e010aae769431be4d3cc50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\neq0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15cc8804d5482ae978d97e7912aa9c768329ad49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=9$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. So the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e96880a2ee1951870033a1cdbeb0ad262f7ac19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) }9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"54\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12\">2001 AMC 12</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2001 AMC 12 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_12_Problems/Problem_13\" t